From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] payloads/external/edk2: Two options of MrChromebox's tree for
 a custom one

The Makefile passes the options of the downstream trees
(FOLLOW_BGRT_SPEC, LOAD_OPTION_ROMS, NETWORK_IPXE, CSMWRAP, LVGL_ENABLE
and the others) to any repository but the official one, and most of
their Kconfig symbols depend on !EDK2_REPO_OFFICIAL accordingly. Two
depend on EDK2_REPO_MRCHROMEBOX instead: EDK2_SECURE_BOOT_DEFAULT_ENABLE
and EDK2_USE_LVGL_RENDERER. A custom repository whose platform has the
same defines, such as upstream edk2 with a package outside the tree that
carries MrChromebox's modules (EDK2_PLATFORM_DSC, EDK2_PACKAGES_PATH),
cannot select them, and its setup loses the LVGL renderer.

Make both depend on !EDK2_REPO_OFFICIAL, as the options they sit with.
Their defaults stay as they are; for MrChromebox's repository nothing
changes. A custom repository without the defines gets LVGL_ENABLE=TRUE
from the default of EDK2_USE_LVGL_RENDERER, which a platform without it
ignores, as it ignores the other downstream options.

TEST=make defconfig of ouroBIOS's W541 configuration with
EDK2_REPO_CUSTOM, EDK2_REPOSITORY the upstream edk2 and the package of
ouroBIOS: EDK2_USE_LVGL_RENDERER=y as with EDK2_REPO_MRCHROMEBOX, and
-D LVGL_ENABLE=TRUE in the build summary. With EDK2_REPO_MRCHROMEBOX the
.config is the same as before.
---
 payloads/external/edk2/Kconfig | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/payloads/external/edk2/Kconfig b/payloads/external/edk2/Kconfig
index ebcac77850..a2ac9f5cb7 100644
--- a/payloads/external/edk2/Kconfig
+++ b/payloads/external/edk2/Kconfig
@@ -300,7 +300,7 @@ config EDK2_SECURE_BOOT_SUPPORT
 
 config EDK2_SECURE_BOOT_DEFAULT_ENABLE
 	bool "Enable UEFI Secure Boot by default"
-	depends on EDK2_SECURE_BOOT_SUPPORT && EDK2_REPO_MRCHROMEBOX
+	depends on EDK2_SECURE_BOOT_SUPPORT && !EDK2_REPO_OFFICIAL
 	help
 	  After EnrollDefaultKeys provisions the default PK/KEK/db/dbx on
 	  first boot, leave Secure Boot enabled instead of forcing it off.
@@ -308,7 +308,7 @@ config EDK2_SECURE_BOOT_DEFAULT_ENABLE
 config EDK2_USE_LVGL_RENDERER
 	bool "Use the LVGL graphical setup renderer"
 	default y if !EDK2_SERIAL_SUPPORT
-	depends on EDK2_REPO_MRCHROMEBOX
+	depends on !EDK2_REPO_OFFICIAL
 	help
 	  Render the firmware setup and boot menu with the LVGL-based
 	  graphical HII display engine (LvglDisplayEngineDxe) instead of the
